 Basic Approach (Always Follow This)
plain
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  1. Read assembly top to bottom         │
│  2. Track eax (return value register)   │
│  3. Ignore setup: endbr64, push, mov rbp│
│  4. Focus on last mov eax before ret    │
│  5. Convert hex → decimal for flag      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
2. Common Instructions
Table
Instruction	Meaning	Example
mov eax, imm	Move value into eax	mov eax, 0x86342
mov eax, [addr]	Load from memory	mov eax, [rbp-0x4]
add eax, val	Add to eax	add eax, 0x1f5
sub eax, val	Subtract from eax	sub eax, 0x65
imul eax, val	Multiply eax	imul eax, 0x4
cmp a, b	Compare a and b	cmp eax, 0x2710
jle label	Jump if ≤	jle 0x5555...
jl label	Jump if <	jl 0x40112c
jmp label	Always jump	jmp 0x401136
ret	Return (eax = result)	—
3. Hex to Decimal (Manual Method)
Example: Convert 0x9fe1a
Table
Position (right→left)	Digit	Decimal	× 16^pos	Result
0	a	10	× 1	10
1	1	1	× 16	16
2	e	14	× 256	3,584
3	f	15	× 4,096	61,440
4	9	9	× 65,536	589,824
Total = 10 + 16 + 3,584 + 61,440 + 589,824 = 654,874
Hex Digit Reference:
plain
0-9 = 0-9
a=10, b=11, c=12, d=13, e=14, f=15
Powers of 16:
Table
Power	Value
16⁰	1
16¹	16
16²	256
16³	4,096
16⁴	65,536
16⁵	1,048,576
